1
00:00:00,270 --> 00:00:03,810
At their evening home gathering, I
announced:

2
00:00:03,810 --> 00:00:08,250
I have decided to be baptized this
coming Sunday and become a Christian.

3
00:00:09,110 --> 00:00:16,490
But the thought that my whole life would
end up in religion made me deeply sad.

4
00:00:17,110 --> 00:00:22,110
I could not help venting my frustration
on these Christians.

5
00:00:22,110 --> 00:00:26,050
Wait, I said. Although I have decided to
be baptized,

6
00:00:26,050 --> 00:00:30,790
I still have three deep regrets that I
want to tell you about.

7
00:00:30,790 --> 00:00:35,150
First, I was raised with a scientific
education.

8
00:00:35,150 --> 00:00:40,036
What I most admired was the motto carved
on my university's administration

9
00:00:40,036 --> 00:00:40,630
building:

10
00:00:40,630 --> 00:00:45,270
You must seek truth, and the truth will
set you free.

11
00:00:45,270 --> 00:00:50,510
You shall know the truth, and the truth
shall make you free.

12
00:00:51,050 --> 00:00:58,210
Yet the Bible you ask me to believe
describes Jesus walking on the sea,

13
00:00:58,210 --> 00:01:02,190
and Jesus rising from the dead. This is
absurd!

14
00:01:02,190 --> 00:01:07,950
Asking me to believe this Bible is
asking me to abandon my pursuit of
truth.

15
00:01:08,770 --> 00:01:13,550
Second, all my life I have loved freedom
and respected others.

16
00:01:13,550 --> 00:01:17,910
So I hate having moral burdens imposed
on me.

17
00:01:18,550 --> 00:01:24,790
Although I am not a Christian, I know
that once I become one,

18
00:01:24,790 --> 00:01:30,650
people will burden me with different
moral standards. They will say:

19
00:01:30,650 --> 00:01:36,030
Aren't you a Christian? Why do you get
angry?

20
00:01:36,030 --> 00:01:41,230
Aren't you a Christian? Why stop your
car on a yellow line?

21
00:01:42,010 --> 00:01:48,290
I have always loved freedom. I really
dislike having moral burdens forced on
me.

22
00:01:48,290 --> 00:01:52,710
The thought of it made me deeply sad.

23
00:01:54,090 --> 00:01:58,490
Third, people in science have a lofty
lifelong goal:

24
00:01:58,490 --> 00:02:05,170
to seek the greatest happiness for
people today and reduce their tears.

25
00:02:05,170 --> 00:02:09,090
So our hearts are not empty.

26
00:02:09,090 --> 00:02:12,743
We are full of love and care for our
fellow human beings, in the horizontal

27
00:02:12,743 --> 00:02:13,230
dimension.

28
00:02:13,890 --> 00:02:20,818
By contrast, Christians seem concerned
only with their relationship with God
and

29
00:02:20,818 --> 00:02:22,810
how much they love Him.

30
00:02:22,810 --> 00:02:27,770
Your love is vertical, but the love of
people in science is horizontal.

31
00:02:28,160 --> 00:02:32,010
Now you want me to turn my horizontal
love into vertical love.

32
00:02:32,010 --> 00:02:35,950
The thought brings me nothing but
sadness.

33
00:02:36,630 --> 00:02:39,150
I poured out all three regrets in one
breath.

34
00:02:39,150 --> 00:02:47,196
Many Christians there had believed for
twenty or thirty years. Suddenly, they

35
00:02:47,196 --> 00:02:48,450
fell silent.

36
00:02:49,790 --> 00:02:52,670
They looked at one another, unsure how
to answer.

37
00:02:53,510 --> 00:03:02,696
After a while, Uncle Geng, a humble
scholar I greatly respected, spoke on
their

38
00:03:02,696 --> 00:03:03,510
behalf.

39
00:03:03,510 --> 00:03:08,688
He said, Asking you to believe in the
Lord does not mean giving up your care
for

40
00:03:08,688 --> 00:03:09,270
humanity.

41
00:03:10,210 --> 00:03:12,490
Second, we are accountable to the Lord.

42
00:03:12,490 --> 00:03:19,114
We need not be overly concerned with
others' moral judgments or the burdens
they

43
00:03:19,114 --> 00:03:20,190
impose on us.

44
00:03:20,190 --> 00:03:23,130
What matters is that you are right with
the Lord.

45
00:03:23,130 --> 00:03:30,830
I could accept that answer, but in my
heart I still felt regret and sadness.

46
00:03:32,840 --> 00:03:36,891
A few days later, still carrying those
three regrets, Liao Shutao kept his

47
00:03:36,891 --> 00:03:38,260
promise and was baptized.

48
00:03:39,460 --> 00:03:43,240
Yet after his baptism, he was not happy
in private.

49
00:03:44,140 --> 00:03:52,586
His wife knew how unhappy he was. Under
even greater pressure herself, she

50
00:03:52,586 --> 00:03:55,440
prayed earnestly for him.

51
00:03:57,230 --> 00:04:01,830
One evening, his wife and child went to
bed as usual.

52
00:04:02,450 --> 00:04:08,030
Unable to sleep, Liao picked up some
gospel testimonies,

53
00:04:08,030 --> 00:04:09,270
for a little diversion.

54
00:04:10,150 --> 00:04:12,910
These were spiritual books he found
easier to read.

55
00:04:13,870 --> 00:04:20,813
They told how different people had
become Christians, and many were
compelling

56
00:04:20,813 --> 00:04:21,970
life stories.

57
00:04:21,970 --> 00:04:31,320
He came across a testimony called A
Shell Collector on the Shore of Truth.

58
00:04:32,080 --> 00:04:39,560
The author was an American named Dudley
Evans. He began:

59
00:04:40,640 --> 00:04:45,500
In the fall of 1970, when I first
arrived at the University of Texas,

60
00:04:45,500 --> 00:04:50,000
I considered myself a hard-core atheist.

61
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:55,870
Liao suddenly felt a joyful sense of
kinship.

62
00:04:56,730 --> 00:04:59,730
This man attended the same university as
I did, he thought.

63
00:05:01,150 --> 00:05:02,370
The account continued:

64
00:05:03,030 --> 00:05:07,190
I entered this university to discover
the true meaning of life.

65
00:05:09,270 --> 00:05:13,730
You shall know the truth, and the truth
shall make you free.

66
00:05:16,160 --> 00:05:22,139
Standing before the university building
where this Bible verse was carved, he

67
00:05:22,139 --> 00:05:25,400
recalled repeating those
words—ironically,

68
00:05:25,400 --> 00:05:29,280
vowing that he would find the truth
before leaving the university.

69
00:05:31,740 --> 00:05:35,160
Reading this, Liao leapt to his feet.

70
00:05:35,160 --> 00:05:39,507
He could hardly believe that this
American had attended the very same

71
00:05:39,507 --> 00:05:40,200
university,

72
00:05:40,200 --> 00:05:47,599
walked past the same building, and felt
the same reverence for the words

73
00:05:47,599 --> 00:05:49,140
engraved there.

74
00:05:49,140 --> 00:05:51,360
With his heart pounding, he read on.

75
00:05:51,360 --> 00:05:55,320
The author had searched everywhere for
the meaning and reality of life,

76
00:05:55,320 --> 00:06:01,040
even exploring Eastern philosophy and
religious practices.

77
00:06:01,040 --> 00:06:04,780
Yet these left him feeling even emptier.

78
00:06:04,780 --> 00:06:09,500
In the depths of his emptiness and pain,

79
00:06:09,500 --> 00:06:17,204
Jesus refreshed his heart with a
wonderful, divine anointing, moving him
to

80
00:06:17,204 --> 00:06:17,820
tears.

81
00:06:17,820 --> 00:06:25,240
His personal experience of coming to
believe in the Lord deeply moved me.

82
00:06:25,760 --> 00:06:30,620
More importantly, he concluded with
these words:

83
00:06:30,620 --> 00:06:35,300
From that day in February 1973 until
now,

84
00:06:35,300 --> 00:06:41,704
Christ has become more real within me
each day, and my experience of Him has

85
00:06:41,704 --> 00:06:42,800
grown richer.

86
00:06:42,800 --> 00:06:46,660
To everyone who is still seeking truth,

87
00:06:46,660 --> 00:06:51,878
I recommend the words of the Lord Jesus
engraved on our university's

88
00:06:51,878 --> 00:06:53,720
administration building:

89
00:06:53,720 --> 00:06:58,420
You must seek truth, and the truth will
set you free.

90
00:06:59,560 --> 00:07:02,180
John 8:32.

91
00:07:02,680 --> 00:07:06,780
He went on: This same Jesus also said,

92
00:07:07,400 --> 00:07:09,420
I am the truth.

93
00:07:09,420 --> 00:07:12,120
John 14:6.

94
00:07:12,680 --> 00:07:15,280
Read those two statements together:

95
00:07:15,280 --> 00:07:20,220
You must seek truth, and the truth will
set you free.

96
00:07:21,640 --> 00:07:23,580
I am the truth.

97
00:07:24,580 --> 00:07:30,060
When I read that passage, I was
profoundly shaken.

98
00:07:30,060 --> 00:07:38,460
It felt like a dream. My whole life
until then seemed like a dream.

99
00:07:38,460 --> 00:07:44,331
Years of scientific education had taught
me to appreciate what I considered the

100
00:07:44,331 --> 00:07:46,040
greatest saying of all,

101
00:07:46,040 --> 00:07:49,500
and now I was discovering that Jesus was
the one who had said it!

102
00:07:49,500 --> 00:07:56,940
My past life seemed like a dream. Only
on that day did I truly wake up.

103
00:07:56,940 --> 00:08:01,012
I found myself back at a starting point
I did not recognize, completely at a

104
00:08:01,012 --> 00:08:01,280
loss.

105
00:08:01,940 --> 00:08:07,640
I put down the testimonies and searched
the Chinese Bible.

106
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:12,540
It was true! The Lord Jesus had said
those words in the Gospel of John.

107
00:08:12,540 --> 00:08:17,698
Still unconvinced, I opened the English
Bible. There were the very words

108
00:08:17,698 --> 00:08:19,560
engraved at my university.

109
00:08:20,460 --> 00:08:26,960
At that moment I became so overwhelmed
that I knelt down.

110
00:08:27,710 --> 00:08:31,380
Jesus, I said, I bow before You in
complete admiration!

111
00:08:31,380 --> 00:08:37,280
At that moment, everything seemed
suddenly to become clear.

112
00:08:38,660 --> 00:08:43,820
It was as though Jesus quietly and
silently answered Liao's three
questions.

113
00:08:43,820 --> 00:08:51,205
First, the saying he had admired most,
and thought faith would force him to

114
00:08:51,205 --> 00:08:55,340
abandon, had been spoken by Jesus
Himself.

115
00:08:55,340 --> 00:09:04,973
Second, the moral burdens he hated and
his fear of losing freedom as a
Christian

116
00:09:04,973 --> 00:09:07,140
suddenly vanished.

117
00:09:08,520 --> 00:09:17,191
Jesus Himself was telling him: Seek the
truth—in other words, seek Me—and I will

118
00:09:17,191 --> 00:09:18,600
set you free.

119
00:09:18,600 --> 00:09:25,131
If the true God and Savior of the
universe Himself promised to set him
free,

120
00:09:25,131 --> 00:09:27,280
what did he have to fear?

121
00:09:28,500 --> 00:09:30,800
Third.

122
00:09:30,920 --> 00:09:38,840
The great compassion for humanity he had
prided himself on now seemed like a

123
00:09:38,840 --> 00:09:44,780
child's naive dream before the all-
knowing, almighty God.

124
00:09:46,580 --> 00:09:51,300
He could not even lessen his own wife's
tears. What could he really do?

125
00:09:52,950 --> 00:09:54,290
Suddenly, Liao understood:

126
00:09:54,790 --> 00:10:00,962
Only by showing people how to look to
God and receive Him could they find

127
00:10:00,962 --> 00:10:03,330
genuine peace and happiness.
